            <chunk name="Object" index="41">
              <items count="3">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">ddca21b5-bcc8-5806-85f8-fc0a45ced2e5</item>
                <item name="Lib" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7f0b6a3e-2f4d-4a51-9a1c-3c8e2d5b9e41</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Plot 2D</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="6">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Chart an acoustic parameter (a dot per band, joined by a line), or the time or frequency response of Analyse Impulse Response (a line per channel), on the canvas: one chart per parameter connected, stacked, for every source-receiver pair of Analyse Impulse Response. Choose which parameter to chart with the Select parameter dropdown beside the data input: T30 until you choose, All, or one by name (EDT, T20, T30, C50, C80, D50, DRR, Ts, STI, G, SPL, LF; the opened menu gives each its title, as T30 (Reverberation Time)), and a sentence right of it says what the chosen parameter is; it lists only the parameters connected, so no LF for a response that is not ambisonic; the time and frequency responses are charted whichever is chosen, and with only them connected the dropdown rests. Drag the corner to resize; hover a chart to read its values; Save writes the charts as a PNG image.</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">0d9476f3-4aa1-4459-9200-2961673b8522</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Plot 2D</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Plot2D</item>
                    <item name="chart_height" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">220</item>
                    <item name="chart_width" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">396</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
