                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Auralise the chosen source-receiver pairs: one anechoic sound, chosen on the Anechoic sound dropdown (a bundled recording, or a file loaded with Load...) or a File Path wired to 'sound', convolved with the impulse response of each pair. The signals keep the format of their impulse responses: mono (Simulate Mono), binaural (Simulate Binaural) or ambisonic (Simulate Ambisonics). Choose the level on the body: 'none' (default) keeps the raw level and may clip; 'relative' takes one gain from the sound convolved with every connected pair, not only the chosen ones, so the loudest connected pair would peak at -1 dBFS and a chosen pair keeps its level difference to it; 'individual' brings each signal to -1 dBFS. Save auralisation writes the signals of the chosen pairs as WAV files: choose a folder and a name (take.wav saves take_mic_&lt;r&gt;_&lt;s&gt;.wav, with r and s the receiver and source indices, as take_mic_0_0.wav, take_mic_0_1.wav, ...). Save RIR writes the impulse responses of the chosen pairs the same way, at the chosen level ('relative' from every connected response) and each with a JSON file of its metadata, including the factor back to its raw level.</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">ec6b5e8c-fdff-405b-82a4-986245d2c8e3</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Auralise</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Auralise</item>
                    <item name="choice_level" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">relative</item>
                    <item name="control_inputs_hidden" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">source_idx
receiver_idx
sound</item>
                    <item name="control_inputs_shown" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="control_value_receiver_idx" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">1</item>
                    <item name="control_value_sound" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">female_speech</item>
                    <item name="control_value_source_idx" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">1</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="3">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>1765</X>
