                        </item>
                      </items>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_input" index="0">
                      <items count="8">
                        <item name="Access" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">2</item>
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">ImpulseResponse object(s), as Simulate gives them, one per source-receiver pair. Sources and receivers are numbered over the responses as connected, in the order they come: the n-th distinct source (receiver) is source (receiver) n, so a filtered or reordered list renumbers the pairs. The 'relative' level takes its gain from every pair connected here.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">598e1e23-4af0-4052-aebf-11a099974c88</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">irs</item>
