            <chunk name="Object" index="52">
              <items count="3">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">ebf0dfa8-2bf3-5fd2-b59e-5ac8fb327480</item>
                <item name="Lib" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7f0b6a3e-2f4d-4a51-9a1c-3c8e2d5b9e41</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Audio Player</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Show and play a signal from Auralise, an impulse response (e.g. one of the irs of a Simulate component), or an audio file: a lane per channel (the body grows with the channels), with a Play/Pause button, Stop, Normalize (scale the signal to full level; off by default, so auralisations play at their rendered level), a click in the waveform to seek, and a volume slider. Drag the corner to set the width and the lanes' height. A file plays whole, without pause or seek. A signal of more than two channels (ambisonic) is shown but not played.</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">17906dbc-1b53-47a6-8514-54a5e206e020</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Audio Player</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Player</item>
                    <item name="gain_db" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="lane_height" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">50</item>
                    <item name="normalize" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="width" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">240</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
